<article class="env-lemma" id="01EP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01EP">Lemma <span data-tag="01EP">20.11.1</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a ringed space. Let $\mathcal{U} : U = \bigcup _{i \in I} U_ i$ be an open covering. Let $\mathcal{I}$ be an injective $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \check{H}^ p(\mathcal{U}, \mathcal{I}) = \left\{  \begin{matrix}  \mathcal{I}(U) 

&  \text{if} 

&  p = 0 

\\  0 

&  \text{if} 

&  p > 0 

\end{matrix} \right.  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      An injective $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module is also injective as an object in the category $\textit{PMod}(\mathcal{O}_ X)$ (for example since sheafification is an exact left adjoint to the inclusion functor, using Homology, Lemma <a href="/tag/015Z" data-tag="015Z">12.29.1</a>). Hence we can apply Lemma <a href="/tag/01EN" data-tag="01EN">20.10.5</a> (or its proof) to see the result. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>